# Copy to .env (untracked) and fill in.
# Domain served by the local traefik with a wildcard certificate; the app answers on grill-room.<DEV_DOMAIN>.
DEV_DOMAIN=local.example.com
# The local traefik's file-provider rules directory (watched).
TRAEFIK_RULES_DIR=/path/to/traefik/rules
GRILL_ROOM_PORT=7680
GRILL_ROOM_METRICS_PORT=7681
# Host address the app port is published on; `make dev-up` defaults it to the docker bridge gateway.
# GRILL_ROOM_BIND=
# LiveKit API key pair, shared by LiveKit, the room server and the STT worker.
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY=API$(openssl rand -hex 6)    LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
# Service token the STT worker presents to the room server: openssl rand -hex 24
STT_TOKEN=
# Service token the tts pod presents to the room server (spec 013): openssl rand -hex 24
TTS_TOKEN=
# Pins the admin token (the voice e2e tests need it): openssl rand -hex 24
GRILL_ROOM_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# Host port (loopback) for the STT worker's /healthz and /metrics.
# STT_METRICS_PORT=7682
# Hugging Face read token file for `make tts-image` (spec 013): its account accepted Kyutai's terms for
# the gated Pocket TTS weights. A BuildKit secret only; the tts image goes to a private registry.
# HF_TOKEN_FILE=/absolute/path/to/hf-token
# Registry `make sandbox-push` pushes the sandbox image to, as <registry>/grill-room/sandbox:<version>.
# REGISTRY=registry.example.com
# Digest-pinned sandbox image the room server advertises to daemons; `make sandbox-push` prints it.
# Empty: each daemon builds the sandbox image from the Dockerfile it embeds.
# GRILL_ROOM_SANDBOX_IMAGE=registry.example.com/grill-room/sandbox:v0.0.0@sha256:<64 hex>
# Lab deployment (deploy/k8s/, make k8s-*). Hosts: grill-room, grill-room-livekit and grill-room-turn
# under K8S_DOMAIN; traefik must hold a certificate for them.
# K8S_DOMAIN=lab.example.com
# PostgreSQL the room server stores in (spec 017), reached directly, no pooler. Service host name.
# K8S_PG_HOST=postgres-rw.databases.svc
# Port; default 5432.
# K8S_PG_PORT=5432
# Database, owned by the login role and created with C collation.
# K8S_PG_DATABASE=grill_room
# Secret in the lab namespace holding the login role as keys username and password.
# K8S_PG_SECRET=grill-room-postgres
# Namespace the database pods run in, opened by the room server's egress policy.
# K8S_PG_NAMESPACE=databases
# require (default), or verify-full once the pod trusts the cluster's CA.
# K8S_PG_SSLMODE=require
# Digest-pinned images; `make k8s-push` prints both lines.
# GRILL_ROOM_IMAGE=registry.example.com/grill-room/server:v0.0.0@sha256:<64 hex>
# GRILL_STT_IMAGE=registry.example.com/grill-room/stt:v0.0.0@sha256:<64 hex>
# GRILL_TTS_IMAGE=registry.example.com/grill-room/tts:v0.0.0@sha256:<64 hex>
# The lab ingress controller's pod CIDR, whose X-Forwarded-For names the client (empty: the peer).
# GRILL_ROOM_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.42.0.0/16
# SMTP relay for magic links in the lab (empty: email sign-in off). K8S_SMTP_NAMESPACE and
# K8S_SMTP_PORT open the room server's egress to it (defaults mailpit and 1025).
# GRILL_ROOM_SMTP_ADDR=smtp.mailpit:1025
# GRILL_ROOM_SMTP_FROM=grill-room <noreply@example.com>
# The lab SMTP relay's mailpit web UI and API, read by `make e2e-lab-mail`.
# K8S_MAILPIT_URL=https://mailpit.lab.example.com
# Prometheus API holding the room server's scrape, which `make k8s-autoscale` scales the tts pod on
# (VictoriaMetrics serves one).
# K8S_PROMETHEUS_URL=http://vmsingle.monitoring.svc:8428
# cosign key pair `make dev-release` signs with (docs/release.md). Keep it out of the repo; the
# password comes from COSIGN_PASSWORD in the environment.
# COSIGN_KEY=/path/to/cosign.key
